From 074067733c38657dbfb7d08b9e69a86489ba8c3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:23:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 39/40] iio: qcom_smgr: decode the report index list, request
 light data

TLV 0x02 of the buffering report is a length byte and one index entry
per requested item (sensor, data type, first sample, sample count,
timestamp, rate). It was decoded as one fixed struct with the length
folded into the first field, which only works for a single item.

Decode it as an array, keep the newest sample of each data type per
sensor, and request the secondary data type as well for the
proximity/light sensor, whose light level is that secondary data. For
that sensor push the proximity count and the illuminance (Q16 lux)
together. Push with iio_push_to_buffers_with_ts() and a scan buffer
that has room for the timestamp.

Also set the default sample rate on every data type: probe set it on
the first one only, once per data type.

Tested on the ZTE Axon 7 (ROHM RPR0521): proximity ~20/s, light ~7/s,
28 lux indoors; accelerometer, gyroscope and magnetometer unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
